n Q3 2026 to 165bp.\n- Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\", so investment-grade names can borrow.\n- Norvane plans to raise 2027 capex by 12%, and Pellham plans 18%.\n- Nothing in the sources shows debt can fund the full plans on its own. There is no data on leverage, credit ratings or total funding needs.\n\n**Equity markets (n6.r1)**\n- Pellham Power withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering because demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n- Pellham says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. The equity shortfall is already reducing capex.\n- I found no data on utility share prices or valuations, and don't know whether Pellham will retry the offering.\n\n**Bottom line**\n- Expect 2027 capex to be funded mainly by debt at higher cost.\n- Stretched utilities like Pellham will probably defer or scale back spending. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment, so this matters for equipment demand.\n- That Pellham can't fill the gap with debt is my inference from its decision to cut orders rather than borrow more. The sources don't state it.","ttft_ms":2197,"type":"result","duration_ms":28290,"uuid":"761c2a8c-53be-42ab-91d3-afb4fc4908aa","ttft_stream_ms":1745,"time_to_request_ms":197,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":20,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":50,"input_hooks":14,"conversation_append":8,"transcript_persist":21,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":16,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":3,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":12,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":64,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":73,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":196,"process_ano